{
  "an6.25:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 6.25 ",
  "an6.25:0.2": "3. Unsurpassable ",
  "an6.25:0.3": "Topics for Recollection ",
  "an6.25:1.1": "“Mendicants, there are these six topics for recollection. ",
  "an6.25:1.2": "What six? ",
  "an6.25:1.3": "Firstly, a noble disciple recollects the Realized One: ",
  "an6.25:1.4": "‘That Blessed One is perfected, a fully awakened Buddha, accomplished in knowledge and conduct, holy, knower of the world, supreme guide for those fit for training, teacher of gods and humans, awakened, blessed.’ ",
  "an6.25:1.5": "When a noble disciple recollects the Realized One their mind is not full of greed, hate, and delusion. ",
  "an6.25:1.6": "At that time their mind is quite unswerving. They’ve left behind greed; they’re free of it and have risen above it. ",
  "an6.25:1.7": "‘Greed’ is a term for the five kinds of sensual stimulation. ",
  "an6.25:1.8": "Relying on this, some sentient beings are purified in this way. ",
  "an6.25:2.1": "Furthermore, a noble disciple recollects the teaching: ",
  "an6.25:2.2": "‘The teaching is well explained by the Buddha—apparent in the present life, immediately effective, inviting inspection, relevant, so that sensible people can know it for themselves.’ ",
  "an6.25:2.3": "When a noble disciple recollects the teaching their mind is not full of greed, hate, and delusion. … ",
  "an6.25:2.4": "",
  "an6.25:2.5": "",
  "an6.25:2.6": "",
  "an6.25:3.1": "Furthermore, a noble disciple recollects the Saṅgha: ",
  "an6.25:3.